  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Beat a player before you score",
  "description": "Play 3 v 3 with keepers in an area of about 25 × 20 metres. One extra rule: before a team can score, someone in the team must have dribbled past an opponent. The coach shouts \"Now!\" when it has happened, and then the team may shoot.\n\nMake it easier with 2 v 2 and a bigger area. Progression: the player who beat the defender may not score themselves – they must pass to a teammate. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Be brave – dribble straight at the defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close and change pace as you go past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Watch the ball while you dribble and look up afterwards."
    }
  ],
